  "title": "Laozi",
  "summary": "Laozi, 'Old Master', is the figure traditionally credited with the Daodejing and honoured as founder of Daoism. Chinese sources place him in the sixth century BCE; Sima Qian's biography makes him a Zhou archivist from Chu who met Confucius. Some modern scholars regard him as entirely legendary.",
